Clips keep their start time and only borrow forward (gap_after), never start earlier: segment start = first word onset, so keeping it preserves sync with the speaker's mouth (#9), and forward-only borrowing makes 'no overlap' a local guarantee (end <= next.start - min_gap) without coordinating neighbours. Silence trimming comes first because F5's fixed-length output carries 0.3-0.9 s of edge silence; after trimming every real clip fit, so the 0.9x slow-down fills slots instead of leaving gaps. Re-translation is behind a regenerate callback (make_regenerator) so fit.py stays independent of translators/TTS, and it is None for MT backends that cannot shorten. Final hard truncate to the window is deliberate: rubberband output length is not sample-exact.
